From 9ec6136f87beb92389cdad03c7d257cf806b5cb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:36:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper_About: credits, build provenance and support page

Reached from a signet at the FOOT OF THE RAIL in both chrome pages - not the
topbar, which is a nowrap flex row whose intrinsic width floors the whole
document (standing rule 44, the overflow bug v2.4.5 fixed).

The page leads with what the project can actually prove: patch count, upstream
base pin and build date, with the three commands to rebuild the image, directly
above the donation ask. Those figures come from /reaper_provenance.js, which the
BUILD stamps - hardcoding them would have the page confidently showing the wrong
patch count one release later, and on a page arguing 'you can verify this' a
stale number is worse than none. Absent or empty renders as a dash.

Credits to RMerlin, ExtremeFireTop, RollOn51, Ripshod, Dave14305, Marchcat2008 &
Unisoft, jb68 and the SNBForums testers; notes to ASUS and Broadcom; GPLv2,
vendor-blob and no-affiliation legal footer - the last because the page carries a
distribution pitch to ASUS and a Broadcom mention.

Hero art is the real brand emblem extracted from RLogo.png, not a hand-drawn
glyph. The rail signet is a scythe with NO enclosing ring: a straight stroke
crossing a ring is the universal prohibition symbol and the first draft read as
'no entry'.

Registered in reaper_inject.c reaper_native[] - own theme, no in-page
self-bounce, so it must bounce a direct hit into the shell WITHOUT getting the
stock reaper_content.css. Skipping that registration is the v2.1.9 audit bug
class.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
